From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emuTOS-MCD <darekadumon@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 23:51:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 094/185] segacd: a watchdog on level 2, and a probe that can
 name the culprit

The console answered the last build with i4 1 -- one level 4 for the
whole visit, then silence, thirteen visits running, where emulation
takes twenty-odd. That number has two completely different meanings and
the counter could not separate them.

So the visit runs in two phases. Phase A puts our own acknowledge in the
level-4 vector: wait out DRS, take the ten status bytes, write $04 back
-- the sequence EmuTOS's own handler uses, which keeps this machine's
drive talking at 75 Hz for minutes at a time. Half a second, then the
count is frozen. Phase B installs the firmware's handler and reads. The
diagnostic prints own/total: equal means Sega's handler is what silences
the drive, diverging means the path is fine and the fault is further in.

The stage-1 gate is retired. It was refusing to call the one function
whose job is to put a drifted drive back in step, on the grounds that
the drive might have drifted. What makes that safe:

  - A watchdog on level 2. Every BIOS call is a jsr with no timeout on
    our side, which is how the console came to sit on a version banner
    with nothing to print. The Genesis raises MDINT every frame whatever
    the drive is doing, so the visit is bounded by a clock the CD cannot
    stop: 300 frames and it is abandoned where it stands -- frame
    discarded, stack reset, stage 5, out through the normal exit.
    EmuTOS's stack pointer moved from a6 into the state block for it;
    a6 no more survives a BIOS call than d0 does.

  - Six failures with no successful read and the timeshare stands down.
    Our own driver takes the drive back. An imperfect D: beats a machine
    that grinds.

Also: CDBCHK returns the carry, not d0, so "probe 007f" stops being a
number that means nothing. $FF8033/$FF8037 are photographed on entry and
printed. The gate array now passes exactly CDD, CDC and MDINT, and the
claim that OR-ing the mask in was measurably faster is withdrawn -- that
comparison was confounded with the $5F7C fix and was not like for like.

The diagnostic engages the timeshare on its own: Right and Down together
is a diagonal, and you cannot tell whether it registered.

Both cores, Down alone: gpgx 83 reads 12 failures, PicoDrive 85/11, all
four D: calls returning and the file's contents coming back. Watchdog
never fires in emulation. Plain boot unchanged.
